WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.829
Step 1. Start the return.

1.2
00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:06.188
Here you record medicines that a patient brings back to the pharmacy.

1.3
00:00:06.188 --> 00:00:08.336
Open the completed dispense order,

1.4
00:00:08.336 --> 00:00:12.310
and select Medication Return at the bottom of the page.

2.1
00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.339
Step 2. Create the return.

2.2
00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:19.400
Care fills in the Name with Medication Return and the name of the patient.

2.3
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.308
The Note is optional. Select Create Return.

3.1
00:00:24.308 --> 00:00:26.770
Step 3. Add the returned items.

3.2
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.623
Select Load from order, tick each item that the patient brings back,

3.3
00:00:31.623 --> 00:00:42.159
and select Done. Enter the Quantity returned, then select Save.

4.1
00:00:42.159 --> 00:00:44.300
Step 4. Approve the return.

4.2
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.691
Select Mark as Approved, which is available after you save at least one item.

4.3
00:00:49.691 --> 00:00:52.432
Care sets the return to Pending.

5.1
00:00:52.432 --> 00:00:54.505
Step 5. Receive the items.

5.2
00:00:54.505 --> 00:00:59.624
Select Receive & Update Stock, choose Completed and Normal, then Confirm.

5.3
00:00:59.624 --> 00:01:07.250
Care puts the items back into the stock of the pharmacy location.

6.1
00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.156
Step 6. Complete the return. Select Mark as Completed.

6.2
00:01:11.156 --> 00:01:13.457
Care sets the return to Completed,

6.3
00:01:13.457 --> 00:01:18.358
and creates and issues a refund invoice on the patient's account.

7.1
00:01:18.358 --> 00:01:20.441
Step 7. Print the return.

7.2
00:01:20.441 --> 00:01:25.282
Care lists the items of the completed return under Items Returned.

7.3
00:01:25.282 --> 00:01:28.202
Select Print to print the return.
